To rationalize the denominator of $\displaystyle\frac{21}{\sqrt{21}}$, we need to get rid of the square root in the denominator. We can do this by multiplying the numerator and denominator by the square root of 21.

\begin{align*}
\frac{21}{\sqrt{21}}&amp;=\frac{21\cdot \sqrt{21}}{\sqrt{21}\cdot \sqrt{21}}\\
&amp;=\frac{21\cdot \sqrt{21}}{21}\\
&amp;=\sqrt{21}
\end{align*}
Therefore, the rationalized form of $\displaystyle\frac{21}{\sqrt{21}}$ is $\boxed{\sqrt{21}}$.

